var AGS=[
['1. Credit Repair Service Agreement',[
'This agreement is between {C} (“Client”) and {B} (“Company”), {BA}.',
'What the Company will do:',
'#1. Review the Client’s credit reports from the credit reporting agencies and identify information that appears inaccurate, incomplete, unverifiable or out of date, then explain the steps the Client needs to take alongside the Company to dispute that information.',
'#2. Prepare the letters and other correspondence needed to dispute that information on the Client’s credit reports.',
'#3. Follow the Client’s progress with Equifax, Experian and TransUnion. Guidance and support may be given by meeting, webinar, video call, phone, email or any other means during normal business hours.',
'What the Client will pay:',
'#1. Initial document processing fee: ${INIT}.',
'#2. Ongoing service fee: ${MON}, charged every 30 days beginning 30 days after the initial fee. This covers the continuing work described in this agreement.'
]],
['2. Your Journey with {B}',[
'{C} understands that working with {B} follows these steps.',
'Step 1. Free consultation. Before signing, I received a free, no-obligation consultation where {B} looked at my credit situation and confirmed it could help.',
'Step 2. Signing. By signing, I allow {B} to begin the services described above, including the fees listed.',
'Step 3. Identity and documents. I will provide what is needed to confirm who I am and to access my reports: a government-issued photo ID, proof of address, and access to my credit monitoring.',
'Step 4. Work begins. When the documents are in, {B} reviews my reports, finds items that look inaccurate, outdated or unverifiable, and prepares and sends disputes to the credit bureaus and, where needed, the companies that report to them.',
'Step 5. Ongoing service. My monthly fee covers the continued work on my file: following up on earlier disputes, escalating items that are not resolved, and sending new disputes as my reports change.',
'Step 6. Ongoing support. I can use {B}’s client portal to follow my progress, and {B} will be available for credit-building guidance while this agreement is active.'
]],
['3. Authorization for Credit Repair Action',[
'#1. I, {C}, called the “Client” here, authorize {B}, {BA}, to prepare, send, receive, sign and deliver the applications, letters and other documents that are needed to work on my credit. This applies to TransUnion, Experian and Equifax, and to any other reporting agency or creditor listed on my reports, as needed to carry out the authority given here.',
'#2. I may cancel this authorization at any time by giving written notice to {B}. Anything done in reliance on it before I cancel is not a breach of my rights. If it is not cancelled sooner, it ends automatically twelve months after the date I sign.',
'#3. {B} may not share or disclose the information it receives about me except as this agreement allows.',
'#4. I give {B} the authority to take the actions that are reasonably needed to work on my credit with the three credit reporting agencies and any other reporting agency or creditor listed on my reports, as I could do myself if I were there in person.',
'#5. I release {B} from claims, demands and damages that arise from the circumstances of this agreement, to the extent the law allows.'
]],
['4. Consumer Credit File Rights Under State and Federal Law',[
'You have a right to dispute inaccurate information in your credit report by contacting the credit bureau directly. However, neither you nor a credit repair company or credit repair organization has the right to have accurate, current and verifiable information removed from your credit report. The credit bureau must remove accurate, negative information from your report only if it is over 7 years old. Bankruptcy information can be reported up to 10 years.',
'You have a right to obtain a copy of your credit report from a credit bureau. You may be charged a reasonable fee. There is no fee, however, if you have been turned down for credit, employment, insurance, or a rental dwelling because of information in your credit report within the preceding 60 days. The credit bureau must provide someone to help you interpret the information in your credit file. You are entitled to receive a free copy of your credit report if you are unemployed and intend to apply for employment in the next 60 days, if you are a recipient of public welfare assistance, or if you have reason to believe that there is inaccurate information in your credit report due to fraud.',
'You have a right to sue a credit repair organization that violated the Credit Repair Organization Act. This law prohibits deceptive practices by credit repair organizations.',
'You have the right to cancel your contract with any credit repair organization for any reason within 3 business days from the date you signed it.',
'Credit bureaus are required to follow reasonable procedures to ensure that the information they report is accurate. However, mistakes may occur.',
'You may, on your own, notify a credit bureau in writing that you dispute the accuracy of information in your credit file. The credit bureau must then reinvestigate and modify or remove inaccurate or incomplete information. The credit bureau may not charge any fee for this service. Any pertinent information and copies of all documents you have concerning an error should be given to the credit bureau.',
'If the credit bureau’s reinvestigation does not resolve the dispute to your satisfaction, you may send a brief statement to the credit bureau to be kept in your file, explaining why you think the record is inaccurate. The credit bureau must include a summary of your statement about disputed information with any report it issues about you.',
'The Federal Trade Commission regulates credit bureaus and credit repair organizations. For more information contact: The Public Reference Branch, Federal Trade Commission, Washington, D.C. 20580.',
'Learn more about the Pennsylvania credit repair laws: [link to the Pennsylvania statutes page, as in your original]'
]],
['5. Pennsylvania Disclosures',[
'Surety bond or trust account. {B} operates as a Credit Services Organization under the Pennsylvania Credit Services Act (73 P.S. §2181 et seq.). As Pennsylvania law requires, the Company maintains a surety bond and/or trust account to protect consumers, and any advance fees collected under this agreement are secured by it. The name and address of the financial institution or surety company are available on written request.',
'No guarantee of results. {B} does not guarantee, promise or warrant any improvement in the Client’s credit profile or score, or the removal of any particular item from the Client’s credit reports. All services follow applicable federal and state law, and results depend on the Client’s situation and how creditors respond.',
'Your rights as a consumer. The Client may get a copy of their credit report from the consumer reporting agencies and may dispute inaccurate information without the help of a Credit Services Organization. The Client confirms receiving every disclosure required by the Pennsylvania Credit Services Act before signing this agreement.'
]],
['6. Notice of Right to Cancel',[
'You may cancel this contract, without any penalty or obligation, at any time before midnight of the 3rd day which begins after the date the contract is signed by you.',
'To cancel, email support@nextupenterprise.com, or deliver a signed and dated copy of this notice or any other written notice to {B}, {BA}, before midnight on the 3rd day after the date you signed. Say: “I hereby cancel this transaction,” then add the date and your signature.'
]],
['7. Acknowledgment of Receipt',[
'I, {C}, confirm with my digital signature that I received the Notice of Right to Cancel and a copy of my Consumer Credit File Rights, and that I understand and agree to what I am signing.',
'Digital signatures: the U.S. Electronic Signatures in Global and National Commerce (ESIGN) Act of 2000 makes electronic records and signatures legally binding, with the same effect as paper documents and handwritten signatures.'
]]
];
